Package: xsmut3d
Title: Somatic Mutations on Predicted Protein Structures Across Species
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Martin", "S.", email = "ms84@sanger.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Projects somatic mutation calls (typically dNdScv 'annotmuts'
    output) for one or more genes onto a three-dimensional protein structure
    retrieved from the AlphaFold Protein Structure Database. Works for any
    Ensembl species: the species protein is aligned to its human ortholog so
    that UniProt functional annotation, COSMIC hotspots and AlphaMissense
    pathogenicity can be transferred across the alignment and reported on the
    structure. Every residue carries its AlphaFold pLDDT confidence and, where
    available, PAE-derived domain confidence, so low-confidence (frequently
    disordered) regions are flagged rather than over-interpreted. Produces an
    interactive 'r3dmol' view, a static two-dimensional domain / lollipop /
    confidence figure, a 3D mutation-clustering test and a tabular report.
    Shares its Ensembl, dNdScv and COSMIC layer with the 'xsmut' package.
